---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { ASK, SITE } from '../lib/site';

const crumbs = [{ name: 'About', href: '/about' }];
---

<Base
  title="About this project"
  description="BetterCalatagan is an independent civic project, not the Municipality of Calatagan’s website: how it works, how figures are checked, licensing and corrections."
  {crumbs}
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="About"
    icon="info"
    title="An independent civic guide"
    lede="BetterCalatagan collects public information about the Municipality of Calatagan, Batangas from government sources, and shows for every figure where it came from and how well it has been checked."
    {crumbs}
  />

  <div class="container wide with-rail page-body">
    <aside class="rail">
      <nav class="rail-nav" aria-labelledby="toc-label" data-spy>
        <p class="rail-title" id="toc-label">On this page</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#independent">Independent</a></li>
          <li><a href="#how">How it works</a></li>
          {ASK.endpoint && <li><a href="#assistant">The assistant</a></li>}
          <li><a href="#privacy">Privacy</a></li>
          <li><a href="#licensing">Licensing</a></li>
          <li><a href="#credits">Credits</a></li>
          <li><a href="#contribute">Corrections</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </aside>
    <div class="prose content">
      <section class="section" id="independent" aria-labelledby="independent-title">
        <h2 id="independent-title">Independent, and not the municipality</h2>
        <p class="statement">{SITE.independence}</p>
        <p>
          It uses its own independent branding. The municipal seal appears solely as a stylised
          historical illustration, not as the site's identity or evidence of government
          authorisation or endorsement. Nothing here is an official statement. For official business, go to the
          municipal hall. Where a figure here and the government document it cites differ, the
          document is authoritative.
        </p>
        <p>
          It is inspired by the <a href="https://bettergov.ph">BetterGov.ph</a> Better LGU community of
          volunteer-built civic sites and is independently maintained.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
        <h2 id="how-title">How it works</h2>
        <p>
          Most civic portals publish a number. This one publishes a number and the evidence behind
          it. Every record carries its sources, the period the data describes, the date a person
          last checked it, how strong the evidence is, and whether it is fit to publish.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Official sources come first.</strong> The Philippine Statistics Authority, the
            Bureau of Local Government Finance and the DILG Full Disclosure Policy Portal are read
            directly. Encyclopaedias, news and social posts can point to a source; they are never
            the source.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The rules are tested.</strong> A record with no source, or verified on a future
            date, or resting only on a weak source, fails the build and cannot be published.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Gaps are shown.</strong> When something cannot be verified — who holds office
            today, the land area — the site says so and explains why, on the
            <a href="/sources#withheld">Sources</a> page.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>History is held to the same standard.</strong> Each sentence on the
            <a href="/history">History</a> page cites its sources; claims we could not verify are
            listed separately rather than retold.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The pages are static, with no accounts, advertising or behavioural analytics.
          The optional assistant uses a separate service and database, described below. The data is
          available as <a href="/data/index.json">open JSON</a>, with the same provenance.
        </p>
        <p>
          The <a href="/resorts">resort directory</a> is a separate, small tourism listing, not a
          government service or a tiered civic dataset. It records links published by resort
          websites, dates its checks and documents booking-scam precautions; it does not verify
          payment accounts or guarantee a safe booking.
        </p>
      </section>

      {ASK.endpoint && (
        <section class="section" id="assistant" aria-labelledby="assistant-title">
          <h2 id="assistant-title">How the assistant works</h2>
          <p>
            Press Enter in any “Ask” box and an AI assistant writes an answer, in English, Filipino
            or Taglish. It is held to the site’s own standard:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>It is instructed to use this site's published evidence.</strong> Every time the site is
              rebuilt, its pages are split into passages and indexed. The assistant is given the
              passages that match your question and is told to answer from them alone, citing each
              one; each citation links to the page it came from.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Complete answers are checked before you see them.</strong> Numeric values
              are compared with the published passages the answer cites, and citation numbers are
              checked. Unsupported figures, listed unverified officials, unapproved contacts and
              certain unsafe claims cause the answer to be replaced. These checks cannot prove
              that every sentence is true or that a figure has been interpreted correctly.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Some questions are never sent to it.</strong> Who holds office today is
              answered with the reason the site does not say, and emergencies with the national 911
              hotline.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            It can still be wrong, as any summary can: the cited page is the authority, not the
            answer. Search works as before, in your browser, and is listed beneath the “Ask” option.
          </p>
        </section>
      )}

      <section class="section" id="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
        <h2 id="privacy-title">Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          BetterCalatagan has no accounts, advertising or behavioural analytics. It sets no
          application cookies{ASK.turnstileSiteKey ? '; the optional Turnstile check uses Cloudflare’s own technology' : ''}.
          Pages are static files; search runs in your browser against a file this site publishes,
          so what you type into search is never sent anywhere.
        </p>
        {ASK.endpoint && (
          <p>
            A question you <em>ask</em> the assistant, along with recent conversation messages and
            the page or document you are viewing, is sent to the assistant’s
            service on Cloudflare and to the AI model provider that writes the answer (NYO, with
            Cloudflare Workers AI as a fallback). Those providers process it under their own terms, potentially outside the Philippines. BetterCalatagan does not save your questions or its answers in any
            database. Its database holds public source passages, temporary request counts tied to
            a daily-changing code derived from your IP address and a random session identifier,
            and daily usage totals. Expired request counts are removed by scheduled cleanup;
            daily usage totals are kept for up to 90 days. Provider logging and retention are
            governed by their own terms and settings; this site cannot promise they keep no copy.
            {ASK.turnstileSiteKey &&
              ' The first time you ask, Cloudflare Turnstile checks that you are not an automated script; it loads only then.'}
            {' '}The conversation is kept in your browser tab until you clear it or close the tab.
            Do not send personal, payment, medical or confidential information to the assistant.
          </p>
        )}
        <p>
          Interactive maps on the overview, <a href="/barangays">Barangays</a> page and barangay
          profiles load outside services.
          When you scroll to it, your browser fetches map tiles from OpenFreeMap and elevation
          tiles from Amazon Web Services, which see your IP address like any website you visit.
          Each map also has a plain outline view that works without those services.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site’s host (Vercel) and assistant host (Cloudflare) may process request metadata,
          including IP addresses, in technical logs for security and operations. Their retention
          depends on provider settings and terms. Document-reader requests also pass through the
          host to DILG or the Internet Archive; opening external links contacts those sites. If you use voice
          input, your browser’s own speech service (in Chrome, Google’s) turns your speech into
          text; the site receives only the text. Questions about your data, or a request to correct
          or remove something that concerns you, are covered by the
          <a href="#contribute">reporting guidance</a> below.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your chosen light or dark theme is stored in your browser’s local storage. The assistant
          also uses tab storage for its session and conversation when enabled. Clearing the
          conversation or your browser data removes the corresponding local records.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="licensing" aria-labelledby="licensing-title">
        <h2 id="licensing-title">Licensing</h2>
        <p>Three different things, three different answers:</p>
        <dl class="licences">
          <div>
            <dt>Code</dt>
            <dd>MIT licence.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>This project’s own compilation</dt>
            <dd>
              Its schemas, annotations, provenance records and written text — including the history
              narrative — are licensed CC BY 4.0.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Government documents and data</dt>
            <dd>
              Not licensed by this project. They remain the works of their issuing agencies under
              Philippine law. We link to them and describe them; we do not relicense them.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <p class="small muted">
          Full terms are in the <a href={`${SITE.repository}/blob/main/LICENSES.md`}>repository</a>.
          The typefaces are Source Serif 4 and Public Sans, both under the SIL Open Font License.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="credits" aria-labelledby="credits-title">
        <h2 id="credits-title">Credits</h2>
        <p>
          The site’s design draws on public references: the
          <a href="https://bettergov.ph" rel="noopener">BetterGov.ph</a> family of
          <a href="https://lgu.bettergov.ph" rel="noopener">Better LGU portals</a>, whose emblem style
          ours follows, and <a href="https://www.america.gov" rel="noopener">America.gov</a>’s
          editorial, answer-first layout. No code, text or images were copied, and the project has
          no affiliation with any of them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Typefaces: Source Serif 4 and Public Sans, both under the SIL Open Font License. Documents
          are read in place with PDF.js.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="contribute" aria-labelledby="contribute-title">
        <h2 id="contribute-title">Corrections and contributions</h2>
        <p>
          Corrections are welcome, especially from people in Calatagan. The one firm rule: every
          civic fact needs a source. An unsourced correction will be declined even if it is right,
          because the project cannot tell the difference.
        </p>
        <p>
          GitHub issues are public. Do not post personal information, identity documents, payment
          records, legal notices or security exploit details there. A private reporting channel
          has not yet been configured; do not submit sensitive material through the public issue form.
          Privacy and removal requests are assessed for urgency and supporting context;
          credible risks may justify restricting an item while it is reviewed. Removal is not automatic.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="button primary" href={`${SITE.repository}/issues/new/choose`}>Report a correction</a>
          <a class="button" href={SITE.repository}>View the source code</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-body {
    padding-block: var(--sp-7) var(--sp-8);
  }
  .section {
    padding-block: 0 var(--sp-7);
  }
  .statement {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--fs-lg);
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    padding: var(--sp-5) var(--sp-6);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--c-bg-alt);
    color: var(--c-ink);
  }
  .section li + li {
    margin-top: var(--sp-3);
  }
  .licences {
    margin: var(--sp-4) 0;
    border-top: var(--border);
  }
  .licences > div {
    padding: var(--sp-3) 0;
    border-bottom: var(--border);
  }
  .licences dt {
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  .licences dd {
    margin: var(--sp-1) 0 0;
    color: var(--c-ink-2);
  }
  .button + .button {
    margin-left: var(--sp-2);
  }
  .button {
    margin-top: var(--sp-2);
  }
</style>
